# Docker does NOT read .gitignore. This file is the only thing standing between a
# `COPY . .` and a real JWT_SECRET, DB_PASSWORD and ADMIN_PASSWORD inside an image
# layer — and a layer is additive, so deleting the file in a later step does not
# remove it. See specs/005-containerise-services/research.md D6.
#
# The build context is this directory (server/), which is where Docker looks for
# this file. A copy at the repository root would be ignored.

# --- secrets: the reason this file exists, first ---
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.pfx
**/*.p12
**/secrets.json

# --- host build output: wrong architecture, and large ---
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/TestResults/
**/*.user
**/*.suo

# --- version control: history contains every secret ever committed ---
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- not needed at runtime ---
**/.vs/
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
**/*.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
start-dev.ps1
start-dev.sh
